# OriginOS default package set — the distro's shopping list.
# One package per line. Most distro work happens HERE, not in code.
# These packages land in the live system (and get installed by the installer).
#
# How to grow this file (your future 90%):
#   1. apt search <thing> on Debian, find the package name.
#   2. Add ONE line, rebuild, boot, check it works.
#   3. If the ISO gets bloated, move extras to a second list file
#      (e.g. origin-extras.list.chroot) so standard stays lean.

# --- base system (keep small, trust Debian defaults) ---
task-laptop
network-manager
sudo
ca-certificates

# --- Origin layer (built from packages/ in this repo, see config/packages/README) ---
origin-desktop
